b82d1a.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued November 1 at 2:20PM MST until November 2 at 10:00PM MST by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...South Central La Plata County in southwestern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1000 PM MST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 218 PM MST, satellite estimates and river gauge data near\nCedar Hill, NM indicate heavy rain in the warned area. Flooding\nis ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nAnimas River, Lightner Creek and Basin Creek.\n\n- At 1:00 PM MST Sunday the stage was 9.5 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise above flood stage\ntonight to a crest of 11.2 feet by early Monday morning. It will\nthen fall below flood stage Monday night.\n- Flood stage is 10.5 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 11.4\nfeet on 06/19/1949.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nDurango and Bondad.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-11-02T22:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"La Plata, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ff90f3bea89f87e4759c63fb880eb38b994db4d6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ff90f3bea89f87e4759c63fb880eb38b994db4d6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-11-02T23:47:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 022347 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 447 PM MST Mon Nov 2 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Rivers across southwest CO and southeast UT remain rain swollen due to runoff. The San Juan River at Pagosa Springs remains in major flood stage. - Light rain below 10000 feet will continue, with snow above. Winter weather highlights continue for the mounta","url":"https://forecast.weather.go